OpenRSP 3.15.2-20: driver and firmware source

Build (Debian / Ubuntu):

  sudo apt install build-essential cmake pkg-config libusb-1.0-0-dev libudev-dev sdcc make
  cmake -S . -B build -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release
  cmake --build build -j

This builds build/libsdrplay_api.so.3.15, build/sdrplay_apiService,
build/src/tools/rsp_info/rsp_info and the RSP bridge firmware from firmware/src:
build/fw_own/fw_common.bin, fw_rsp1.bin and fw_rspduo.bin.

Install:

  sudo cmake --install build && sudo ldconfig
  sudo /opt/sdrplay_api/sdrplay_apiService

The library goes to /usr/local/lib (set -DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX to change it), the service to
/opt/sdrplay_api and the firmware to /usr/share/sdrplay_api/firmware/own. The API headers are
in include/.

The systemd unit, udev rules and hwdb file the released packages install are in system/linux.
Configure with -DSDRPLAY_INSTALL_SYSTEM_FILES=ON to install them as well (to
/etc/systemd/system, /etc/udev/rules.d and /etc/udev/hwdb.d), then:

  sudo systemd-hwdb update && sudo udevadm control --reload && sudo udevadm trigger
  sudo systemctl daemon-reload && sudo systemctl enable --now sdrplay

